===History===
*Arcane Aegis was first introduced in the [[Trial]] mission [[The Jordas Verdict]], which was retired in {{ver|22.14}}.
*The [[Operation: Scarlet Spear]] event sold Arcane Aegis from [[Little Duck]] for 2,000 {{Resource|Scarlet Credits}}.
*The [[Operation: Orphix Venom]] event sold Arcane Aegis from [[Father]] for 400 {{Resource|Phasic Cells}}.
*The [[Operation: Gargoyle's Cry]] event sold Arcane Aegis from the [[Jahu Gargoyle|Vigile Jahu Gargoyle]] for 6 {{Resource|Grotesque Splinter}}.
*The [[Operation: Belly of the Beast]] event sold Arcane Aegis from [[Ordis]] for 5 {{Resource|Volatile Motes}} in the first run of the event, and 6 Motes in the second, with a purchase limit of 42.
*The [[Operation: Eight Claw]] event sold Arcane Aegis from [[Dominus Thrax]] in bundles of 7, costing 4 {{Resource|Dominus Aureus}}, with a purchase limit of 3 (21 Arcanes  total).
*The [[Operation: Blood of Perita]] event sold Arcane Aegis from [[Roathe]] for 4 {{Resource|Marks of Valiance}} with a purchase limit of 21 per week.

==Notes==
*Has a hidden stat that sets shield recharge delay to '''0''' seconds while active. This causes the players shields to constantly regenerate, even when being damaged.
**{{D|Magnetic}} status effect still prevents shield regeneration with this Arcane active.
*Shield Recharge bonus is additive to the innate '''5%''' shield recharge rate.
*Shield recharge bonus stacks multiplicatively with {{M|Fast Deflection}} and {{M|Vigilante Vigor}}.
**A {{WF|Hildryn}} with {{M|Redirection}}, {{M|Fast Deflection}}, and {{Arcane|Arcane Aegis}} equipped will have a shield recharge rate of 
:::{{Math|[ 15 + ( 5% + {{Arcane|Arcane Aegis|30%}} ) * 1780 * ( 1 + {{M|Redirection|100%}} ) ] * (1 + {{M|Fast Deflection|90%}})|t=y|bf-a=y}} shields per second while {{Arcane|Arcane Aegis}} is active.
*Does <u>not</u> generate [[overshields]].
*Since this Arcane only triggers when shields are damaged, it has no benefit on {{WF|Inaros}}, {{WF|Kullervo}}, or {{WF|Nidus}} (as they have no shields to begin with), any Warframe with {{Arcane|Arcane Persistence}} equipped, or during a [[Nightmare Mode]] mission with the ''No Shields'' modifier.

==Bugs==
*Activating Arcane Aegis once will break the 80% Shield Recharge cap for the rest of the mission or until death.
After the cap is lifted, {{WF|Gauss}}'s [[Gauss/Abilities|Passive]], {{WF|Jade}}'s {{A|Symphony of Mercy}}, and {{Focus|Vazarin}} ability {{Focus|Guardian Break}} when paired with {{M|Fast Deflection}} and {{M|Vigilante Vigor}} will set Shield Recharge Delay to 0. Due to Shield Gating, this makes shields effectively impossible to bypass except through Toxin or Magnetic status.


